From: MacWin Compatibility Probe <dev.local.macwin@local>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 04:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize EngineSync IPC state before dataset reset

Wine/Whisky compatibility probing shows a startup fail-fast before the first
EngineRepresentation, JASPEngine, Desktop started, or loadQML milestone. The
observed order is:

  EngineSync::EngineSync
    -> DataSetPackage::setEngineSync
      -> DataSetPackage::reset
        -> DataSetPackage::endLoadingData
          -> DataSetPackage::enginesReceiveNewData
            -> EngineSync::enginesReceiveNewData

Because the call is on the GUI thread, DataSetPackage dispatches directly into
EngineSync while its constructor has not returned yet. Initialize the IPC memory
name before attaching EngineSync to DataSetPackage. This keeps the initial reset
synchronous, before the downstream proxy chain is constructed, while making the
constructor re-entry observe valid EngineSync state.

diff --git a/Desktop/engine/enginesync.cpp b/Desktop/engine/enginesync.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/Desktop/engine/enginesync.cpp
+++ b/Desktop/engine/enginesync.cpp
@@ -93,9 +93,9 @@ EngineSync::EngineSync(QObject *parent)
 	// So lets put it on 500ms...
 	QTimer::singleShot(500, this, &EngineSync::deleteOrphanedTempFiles);
 
-	DataSetPackage::pkg()->setEngineSync(this);
-
 	_memoryName = "JASP-IPC-" + std::to_string(ProcessInfo::currentPID());
+
+	DataSetPackage::pkg()->setEngineSync(this);
 }
 
 EngineSync::~EngineSync()
